  "tagline": "etcd's maintained fork of BoltDB: a simple, pure-Go B+tree store in a single file.",
  "description": "bbolt is the etcd project's fork of Ben Johnson's Bolt, a pure-Go embedded key-value store modelled on LMDB. Data lives in one memory-mapped file as a copy-on-write B+tree organised into nested buckets, with fully serializable transactions: many concurrent readers and a single writer. Because it is small, dependency-free and crash-safe, it is the storage engine under etcd (and therefore Kubernetes) and is widely used by Go tools such as Consul's Raft log store and InfluxDB 1.x. It is best for read-heavy, moderate-size data; heavy random writes are slow compared with LSM engines.",
